.TH FL-FIREWALL 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-firewall \- firewall settings for fldesktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-firewall\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configures \fBfirewalld\fR(1): the default zone, panic mode (which blocks all
network traffic and is announced with a notification), and for each zone
the allowed services, open ports, the network interfaces and source
addresses that belong to it, masquerading and port forwarding.
.PP
Changes apply at once. With \fBSave changes permanently\fR (the default)
they are also written to the permanent configuration, so they survive a
reload and a restart; without it they last until the next reload.
\fBReload\fR drops changes that were made only for now, \fBKeep Current
Rules\fR saves the running rules as the permanent ones.
.PP
The same view is the Firewall page of \fBfl-settings\fR(1). Administrator
rights are asked for by \fBfl-polkit-agent\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfirewall-cmd\fR(1), \fBfirewalld\fR(1), \fBfirewalld.zones\fR(5)
